      <h1>Ming Dynasty Hanfu Style: Structured, Beginner-Friendly, and Universally Flattering</h1>
      <p class="lead" style="font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--color-muted);margin-top:1.5rem;line-height:1.55;">
        Ming Dynasty Hanfu is the most popular style in the global Hanfu community today -- and for good reason. The iconic mamianqun (horse-face skirt) creates a structured, A-line silhouette that flatters every body type. Adjustable waist ties mean no hard-to-fit sizing. And the mix-and-match potential is nearly infinite.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0;">
